    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602-a5">

                <pb facs="0732" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg658"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Subenclosure 4—Document E]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Commissar for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chicherin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American Consul
                        at Moscow</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Poole</hi>: It is unfortunately impossible for me as yet to
                    give you a definite answer about the possibility of departure through Archangel.
                    It is in consequence necessary to delay any action in the sense indicated in
                    your letter of to-day until the situation in Archangel is such as to make the
                    possibility of departure unquestionable.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Chicherin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
